What Is Not in This Repository
------------------------------
1. No M-VAVE / Sinco firmware, keys, or software binaries:
   Official firmware update packages (`SMC-PAD_005.fwsc`),
   device/image keys, vendor configuration and OTA applications (`Midi Suite`,
   `CubeSuite`, `SincoOTA`), vendor manuals (`SMC-PAD_ZE.pdf`), and per-device
   flash dumps are NOT included or distributed in this repository. Users
   building custom firmware supply their own downloaded stock `.fwsc` locally.

2. No JieLi SDK source code or compiler toolchain binaries:
   This repository does not redistribute Zhuhai Jieli Technology's SDK
   (`fw-AC63_BT_SDK`), precompiled SDK libraries, or x86-64 compiler/post-build
   binaries. `firmware/builder/setup_toolchain.py` fetches the publicly
   published JieLi SDK and toolchain directly from upstream at build time, and
   `firmware/sdk_overlay/apply.py` applies our clean-room C drivers, USB/BLE
   MIDI stack, and sequencer code on top of a local working copy.

3. Note on redistributing compiled `.ufw` / `.fwsc` firmware images:
   A compiled firmware image links against libraries from JieLi's
   `fw-AC63_BT_SDK` and, when packaged for stock SincoOTA compatibility via
   `repack_oldchain.sh`, incorporates the user's stock second-stage bootloader
   (`uboot.boot`) and RCSP OTA loader (`ota.bin`). Check the applicable
   upstream license terms before redistributing prebuilt binary images.

4. Note on USB VID:PID (`1209:0001`):
   `firmware/sdk_overlay/apply.py` configures the USB device descriptor with
   VID:PID `1209:0001` (the pid.codes open-source USB VID `0x1209` and its
   reserved local-testing PID `0x0001`) so that vendor updater and editor
   utilities do not mistake custom test builds for stock firmware. Per
   https://pid.codes/1209/0001/, PID `0x0001` is reserved for local testing
   only; if you distribute prebuilt firmware binaries publicly, allocate a
   dedicated pid.codes PID or configure your own VID:PID.

